<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for May 8.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for May 8.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Wednesday announced the following forecasts and data for UK gas consumption in the period May 6 to 8.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>May 6 (actual) 235 mcm, 55 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 7 (forecast) 248 mcm, 58 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 8 (forecast) 237 mcm, 55 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = Seasonal Normal temperature)</p>
<p>May 6 (actual) 4.9 Celsius, SNT 11.9 Celsius</p>
<p>May 7 (forecast) 6.1 Celsius, SNT 12.0 Celsius</p>
<p>May 8 (forecast) 7.5 Celsius, SNT 12.1 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called for Wednesday, with none expected on Thursday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
